WEBVTT

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.510
<i>My name is Ichiro Marukobi.</i>

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:12.900
<i>They say that there are three other people 
in the world that look just like you,</i>

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.080
<i>but in my case, there are quite a few.</i>

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.200
<b>Hot Lunches</b>

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.490
Thanks for waiting.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.960
<i>I must be special...</i>

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.400
<i>But up until now, 
nothing good has happened to me.</i>

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.550
Huh?

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.790
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:37.040
Wh-Who are you?

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.220
Oh, stop kidding around. 
Let's hurry up and go.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.720
Huh? Go?

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:43.950
Wait...

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.590
Wait. I think you've got the wrong person...

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.340
You're late.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.500
Sorry!

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.070
I thought you weren't going to come.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.330
Of course I came.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.570
<i>Crap... This isn't good.</i>

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.870
Now, let's get started...

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:07.790
...with this mixer.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.180
<i>M-M... Mixer?!</i>

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.770
<b>Capture That Face</b>

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.850
This SPH...

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.440
It's like when I was playing 
in a grassy field when I was a child.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.790
It's a kind scent that I love.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.490
It feels warm and refreshing.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.360
All clear.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.000
Is there anything else bugging you?

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.490
Not really.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:15.290
For example, are there any instances where 
there's some SPH that never caught your attention,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.260
but now it suddenly 
makes you uncomfortable?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.120
Eh?

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.880
<i>Meaning, do any of them smell bad?</i>

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.710
Like Officer Kokonose's SPH.

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:26.000
How did you...

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:32.120
I had him confess. His SPH's accuracy 
and intensity have increased.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.650
It's like he's matured a little 
after updating.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.900
It's fine. I can endure 
Officer Kokonose's smell.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.640
It doesn't affect my work.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.140
Calm down, Misuzu. 
We're not trying to take your job.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.030
But...

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.910
Could you just tell us honestly? 
I'm very interested in this.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.260
Right.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.910
When Officer Kokonose showed me 
the updated Monitalien...

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.650
I smelled something very strong 
and foul from his SPH.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.640
A smell so powerful that it went up my nose, 
and it felt like my brain was going to split.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:16.140
It's very hard to stand in front 
of him without wearing nose plugs.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:20.400
I see... I might've been able to 
narrow down the possible reasons.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.640
Use this.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.290
It's a hairpin-type SPH curtain.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.650
It will cut down specific SPH 
just by having it on.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.150
What's the matter?

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.470
Is there any other design?

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:38.020
It's not my style. It looks very childish.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.620
What do you have on, Misuzu?

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.090
N-Nothing... It's just a hairpin.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.050
So that's the kind of thing you're into.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.510
Is there a problem with that?

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:02.100
Not really... just, the 
fairy-tale look is surprising.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.250
Actually, it's pretty childish.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.840
I-I don't think it's weird.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:12.710
I totally understand wanting 
to change up your hairstyle.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.660
But I...

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.160
My battle suit is rather 
revealing and embarrassing...

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.040
So I don't think I could change 
my hairstyle enough to cover up all of that.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.790
Come to think of it...

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.540
Officer Kokonose saw you the other day.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.680
Now, time for work.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:34.000
I see. So you encountered a purse snatcher.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.390
Was there anything in your bag?

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.930
So it was a kidnapping attempt?

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:41.250
There was a groper!

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.770
P-Please calm down...

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.730
Someone poked my elbow.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.780
To us, our elbows are 
like boobs to you Earthlings!

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.530
B-Boobs?!

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:52.660
W-Well, we're now going to make 
a composite sketch of the suspect...

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.200
I don't want you! I'll leave it to 
this handsome fellow over here.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:56.950
Huh?

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.950
Leave it to me, chu!

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:05.780
Chuta! Misuzu's looking over here.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:06.290
Huh?

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.300
Good morning.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.330
G-Good morning.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.210
Chuta! Misuzu's not wearing nose plugs.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:22.070
Sonokata! If you don't wear 
nose plugs, my smell...

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.560
What about it?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.590
Huh? Well...

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:30.330
The nose plugs were just an accessory, 
and had nothing to do with any smells.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.820
<i>Seriously? Then I just had the wrong idea?</i>

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:35.380
I don't stink?

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:36.380
You do not.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:37.720
Really?

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:38.820
Yes.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.070
<i>What was I so worried 
about this whole time?!</i>

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:46.080
Huh? It's rare for you 
to wear something like that...

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.880
Yes, I know it's childish!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:49.470
Huh?

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:52.930
I mean... I'm just not very fond of it.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.540
Why are you wearing it if you don't like it?

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.380
For my appearance...

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.580
Your appearance?

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:01.300
It doesn't matter. Please leave it alone.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:05.310
<i>Actually, it looks nice on her...</i>

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:08.310
Yes, just like that.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:11.400
I'm sorry I'm late, 
Assistant Inspector Chips.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:14.230
I was just finishing up a composite 
sketch of a groper, chu.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.230
So something like this, chu?

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:19.740
I saw that face in another division...

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:20.990
Chu?

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:22.850
It's the purse snatcher.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:24.080
They look exactly alike.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.860
A baby kidnapping case.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.080
The same...

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:32.260
Purse snatching, kidnapping, and groping...

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.460
To think that the composite sketches 
were all the same for three different cases...

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.310
Does that mean it's the same person?

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:43.390
I'll try searching for this face among
 the composite sketches in our database.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.140
Huh? It can't be...

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:50.400
Hey, what's going on?

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.560
I conducted a search for a person 
who matches this facial data

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:58.000
in Shizuoka Prefecture, where the incidents 
happened, and 152 people showed up.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.470
Why are there so many?

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:02.500
That's because when aliens 
like the Dunians,

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.580
who don't have transformation 
abilities, come to Earth,

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.880
they are required to get cosmetic surgery 
to look like an Earthling for a while.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.340
Yeah but they don't need to 
all have the same face...

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.400
The Dunian government is pretty lax, so...

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.590
I'll send them a stern warning about that.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:21.010
But this isn't good, chu.

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:25.360
If the culprit is among them, it's going 
to be really hard to find them, chu.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:27.320
Were there any specific features 
other than their faces?

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:31.140
In all three cases, the suspect was 
wearing a red hoodie and jeans.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:33.740
Was there a SPH signal at the crime scenes?

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:38.030
Just like Earthlings, they don't emit SPH,

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:41.840
so we have no other choice but to 
interrogate those 152 people.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:47.260
Um... I want to make dinner at home, 
so will I be able to go home by then?

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.360
Not happening, chu.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.010
But this is for peace 
throughout the galaxy, chu.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.880
Right. That's the spirit!

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.630
I'm leaving the interrogations to you guys.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:55.350
Huh?

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:58.170
This in an incident involving three divisions 
of the investigations department, chu.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.920
We have to all work together, chu.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:05.090
Well, Misuzu from Division 2 was the first one to 
realize this, so I don't want to steal her thunder.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:03.920
Yup, yup.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:08.800
Chuta, it's very apparent that 
no one wants to do this.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.730
Well, we're counting on you, Misuzu.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.660
We won't be able to do this alone, chu!

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:15.230
<i>Investigations department.</i>

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:18.250
<i>There was an arson incident on Earth, 
and there is a possibility</i>

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.230
<i>that this is an intergalactic incident.</i>

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.980
<i>Can any division rush over there?</i>

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:24.540
Yes! An exciting assignment!

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.860
I'm getting fired up!

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.280
We can't lose, chu.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.360
Of course not.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.280
We'll go!

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:33.780
Let's see. What to do...

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:36.550
If it's an arson case, 
it's better to let Division 2 go.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:37.640
What?

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.290
Why is that?

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:42.050
It hasn't been very long since Veronica 
from Division 5 underwent surgery

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:44.310
from the remote control SPH case,
 and she hasn't fully recovered yet.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:48.750
<i>And I only recently reattached the neck 
and legs of Virgil from Division 1.</i>

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:50.900
But this is nothing.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.480
I guess I do owe you my life...

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:55.850
<i>We're counting on you, 
Investigations Division 2.</i>

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.490
Yoyosa!

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:02.270
I'm pretty certain that Veronica and 
Virgil's wounds have completely healed...

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:05.230
Of course. I'm the one who treated them.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.010
Then why...

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:12.310
I have a feeling that the reason for Officer 
Kokonose's smell is about to become clear.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:25.020
<b>Méliès</b>

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:25.020
<b>Isaac</b>

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:25.020
<b>McClane</b>

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:35.420
Let's go. I believe that smoke 
is coming from the arson site.

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:36.480
Huh?

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.420
The police are here.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:43.700
A lot of intergalactic crimes 
are incidents that Earthlings

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.710
can identify as something that 
would happen in their own society.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:51.660
So they are reported to the police 
pretty often, chu.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:52.910
Let's go.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:55.560
Huh? Where are we going?

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.810
Even if we were to go to 
the crime scene right now,

00:10:57.810 --> 00:10:59.880
we can't get close because 
 the police are there.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:01.680
So we're going to make a stop, chu.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:06.220
Identification complete. 
You may enter the shop.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.910
<i>This is DJ Tommy's reader mail corner.</i>

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:08.700
What is this place?

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:14.780
It's a café where you need an intergalactic 
passport or an ēlDLIVE badge to enter.

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:16.100
<i>The next subject is from radio name: 
Lion Willing to Die-san.</i>

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:18.790
It's a special place where aliens are 
allowed to be in their natural forms.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:19.240
<i>"Hello, DJ Tommy.</i>

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:21.010
Who knew a place like this existed...

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:23.570
<i>I'm troubled because I've been tasked 
with something very important.</i>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.050
Let's start our investigation.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:24.560
Chuta, you go over there, chu.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:29.320
<i>Is there a good way I can 
get out of doing this task?"</i>

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:25.530
Well, then...

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:28.680
We're looking for the suspect 
in an arson incident.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:30.540
We ask for your cooperation 
in the investigation.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:30.520
<i>Well...</i>

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:35.120
<i>I think it's good to try anything with 
everything you've got while you're young.</i>

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.290
What? Investigation?

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.120
If you just tell me anything you know, 
this'll be over quickly.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:36.970
How annoying.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:41.620
<i>As long as that important task doesn't 
involve you becoming a mafia boss or anything.</i>

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:39.410
If you take an uncooperative attitude,

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:41.620
you will be detained on suspicion 
of enabling a criminal's escape.

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:42.800
What?!

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.260
Hold it, Misuzu.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.640
That's going a bit overboard, chu.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:53.640
You can't make an omelet without milk.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.310
Yeah, it makes it so fluffy.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.570
What are you investigating, moo?

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.570
It's an arson...

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:03.020
Oh, the arson that happened nearby.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:05.770
You need to hurry up and answer! Or else...

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:07.840
M-Misuzu, calm down, chu.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.270
S-Sonokata!

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:13.260
You, there...

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:18.220
What are you doing to my darling?

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:19.660
A Melpleian robot!

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.290
No, chu! That's an actual Melpleian, chu!

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.040
I hope you're prepared...

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:30.240
Oh, did you crochet that pouch?

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.460
The cross-stitching is so detailed.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:34.090
You can tell?

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:34.920
Yeah!

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.650
My honey made me this awesome outfit, too.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.400
Wow, you can even make clothes?

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.660
My honey is the best in the universe.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:44.560
We can probably get information 
from them now, chu.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:45.000
Oh, darling...

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.550
An arson?

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:50.060
We're looking for the suspect, chu.

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:55.910
Come to think of it, I saw a man in a red hoodie 
looking around suspiciously near the scene.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.920
A red hoodie!

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:00.850
Could it be this man?

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.080
Yeah, that's the guy.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.510
What's going on, chu?

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:14.640
To think that the arson was also caused 
by the Dunian in the red hoodie...

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:18.350
Purse snatching, 
attempted kidnapping, groping...

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:20.630
And now arson. 
If the suspect had the same face

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:23.770
and was wearing the same thing 
in every incident, then...

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:27.820
There were 152 Dunians that showed up 
at the bureau alone, chu.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.640
Just because they have 
the same face and clothes,

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.820
it won't be enough to determine 
that they're the same person, chu.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.070
Anyway, let's go to the crime scene.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:38.010
It's possible that the 
suspect is still nearby.

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:38.950
Chu?!

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:42.920
Hey, kids. Do you have a moment?

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.210
I have something to ask you.

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:49.050
Did you happen to see 
anyone suspicious nearby?

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:49.840
Just you.

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:53.210
You got me there.

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:56.100
I'm a police officer with 
the Shizuoka prefectural police.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.250
There was a fire nearby.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:03.140
It seems to be an arson incident, 
so we're looking for the suspect.

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:05.330
W-We don't know anything about it.

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.990
We're just passing through.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:10.730
I see. That's good, then.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:14.240
Because they say that suspects 
usually return to the crime scene.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:18.180
Did you guys have some business here?

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:20.760
That's Shirobori Middle School's uniform, isn't it?

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:23.970
That's pretty far from here.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:25.890
U-Um, well...

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.460
He's suspecting you, Chuta.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:27.850
We...

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:29.970
We're on a date.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.640
Well, aren't you a lovely couple?

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.900
But where are you going on said date?

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.380
The movie theater nearby.

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:42.720
We're going to see the rescreening of 
<i>Adults Just Don't Understand</i> at Fujiyama Cinema.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.820
Right, Chu-kun?

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.750
A rescreening of a movie, eh?

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:53.800
Yes. Chu-kun loves that movie.

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:59.990
I see. Just a moment, then. I'm going 
to confirm that it's actually playing.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:57.110
<i>H-H-Her chest...</i>

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:00.370
<i>Sonokata's chest!</i>

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:05.250
All right. Please hurry or we might 
not make it in time for the screening.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:03.380
Your heart is beating too fast, Chuta.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:10.030
Oh, it's definitely playing.

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:11.290
Hidaru-san.

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:14.020
We found someone suspicious.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:18.800
Sorry to bother you two. 
Make sure you don't get home too late.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:20.010
Okay.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.060
That was close, chu.

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.930
Thanks for the movie information.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.940
No problem at all, chu.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:31.060
Is something wrong?

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:34.070
Misuzu, turn around slowly, chu.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.700
That face...

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:43.460
And he's wearing 
a red hoodie and jeans, chu.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:47.080
Let's flank him. I'll go from behind.

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:50.250
Chuta, get ahold of yourself.

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:53.960
I-I can still feel her chest on my arm...

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.760
Lower your heart rate! 
At this rate, you're going to die!

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:59.290
<i>Th-They were so soft...</i>

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.230
Don't you need to carry out your mission?

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:03.680
I-I know.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.680
The suspect's over there, right?

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:10.790
Wha... Crap!

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.720
This is Kokonose. The suspect got away.

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:18.860
What happened, chu?

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:20.680
I was sort of out of it...

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.460
I'm sorry! This is my mistake!

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:26.030
I can't let him escape because of me...

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.300
Dolugh, wings!

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:31.100
Sympathy!

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:40.390
Dolugh, speed up!

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:42.020
Sympathy!

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.620
All right, we can do this!

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:59.730
H-Hey, are you...

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:01.250
What are you doing, chu?

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.790
If you move, I will cut you.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.200
SPH...

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.120
We're the Space Police, ēlDLIVE!

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:13.660
Will you accompany us to the bureau? 
We have a lot of questions for you.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.280
That's...

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:20.000
...my line!

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.860
I have so much I want to tell you!

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:27.860
What's going on, chu?

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:31.720
Your intergalactic passport was stolen?

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.460
Yeah.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:39.480
Without that, I can't prove that I'm a Dunian,
 and I can't report to ēlDLIVE.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:42.130
And because you were panicked,

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:45.780
you tried purse snatching and groping 
so you'd get reported to ēlDLIVE.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:49.030
More importantly, please hurry up 
and catch the culprit.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:52.330
A weird Earthling 
that was at a mixer stole it.

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:54.500
Huh? Earthling?

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:58.370
What's the meaning of this, 
Ichiro Marukobi-san?

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:01.300
Aw, man. I guess I've been found out.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:03.670
It was finally getting interesting, too.

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.560
So why did you steal the passport?

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:11.930
Everything started because I was mistaken 
as someone else and taken to a mixer.

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:17.210
I found out that everyone there other than me 
was an alien, and I was super surprised.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:21.820
And then I borrowed the passport I found there, 
and researched a bunch of stuff.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:25.240
From there, I felt like I was 
the protagonist in a SF movie.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:30.500
I knew there was some important reason 
that I was born with this face!

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:33.490
Finding aliens disguised 
as humans is a huge deal!

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:37.260
I even found out space police existed!

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:40.250
And that settles that, chu.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.720
Sonokata, thanks for earlier.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:44.510
Huh?

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:50.270
We almost lost the suspect 
because of my mistake. Thank you.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:53.280
I-It's nothing...

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:55.780
<i>I wonder what's wrong.</i>

00:18:56.420 --> 00:19:00.090
<i>Usually, she'd say something 
really mean right about now.</i>

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:02.990
Psychogenic?

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:08.320
Perhaps you felt a bit of panic 
when you saw Chuta maturing.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:12.170
He solved a case while you weren't around,

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:15.270
and you felt some pressure 
at the fact that Chuta was maturing,

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:18.770
so your sense of panic 
affected your sense of smell.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:20.470
Th-That's...

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.680
Is there any proof of this?

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:23.630
Yes.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:25.730
Pervert!

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:26.920
Oh, sorry.

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:31.570
Actually, at the point Officer Kokonose 
made a mistake at the scene today,

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:34.140
the SPH curtain stopped working.

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:35.060
What?

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:40.530
You were able to accept the smell 
without the help of the SPH curtain.

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:45.770
I believe that your panic went away 
when he made the mistake,

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:49.350
and your sense of smell 
went back to normal after that.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:50.820
No way...

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:52.670
It's the undeniable truth.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:56.920
Which means... the reason for 
the smell was because of me,

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:02.050
and somewhere in my heart, I was hoping 
that Officer Kokonose would fail.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.360
I'm...

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.090
...the worst!

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:10.040
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.880
You aren't hoping that 
your coworker will fail.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:16.770
What's at the foundation of this is a 
sense of annoyance towards yourself.

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:22.610
When you saw Chuta maturing next to you, 
your urge to mature yourself also intensified.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:25.610
That's a very natural thing.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:31.200
Chuta can also be very mysterious. He's able to 
somehow pull up the people around him.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:33.460
Right.

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:38.330
There's proof that you don't 
actually want him to fail.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:42.030
You should still be smelling 
that bad smell from him just slightly.

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:46.520
I just thought that this device wasn't 
able to completely make it go away...

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:50.010
If that smell was due to someone else's failure, 
there'd be nothing you could do.

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:53.420
This is a scent that 
only your growth can change.

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.920
It may completely disappear someday,

00:20:55.920 --> 00:21:01.740
or perhaps it will become as comforting 
as the smell of a grassy field back home.

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:11.000
Hey, Misuzu. I received a report about the 
arson incident from Chips. Well done.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.700
Chief Laine...

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:14.660
Keep up the good work.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:16.280
Yoyosa!

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:20.580
Oh, also...

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:23.790
That hairpin really suits you.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.300
I have to doubt your sense of style, Chief.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:31.950
That's it. That attitude describes 
you perfectly, Misuzu.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:39.730
<i>The reason for Officer Kokonose's 
smell was completely me...</i>

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:44.980
I'm counting on you.

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:46.350
Yoyosa!

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:50.240
Hey, you're here.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:51.610
Pardon me...

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:29.350
Chief Laine! The Red Bean Paste 
Mochi Galaxy lies before us!

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:31.180
What?! That's an emergency!

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:35.000
We have to eat all of it 
before they go bad! Oh, man!

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:36.350
Next time on <i>ēlDLIVE,</i>

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:37.890
"Your Voice..."

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time
Your Voice...</b>

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.090
It was only a dream...
